"e8479ff8-f732-4acd-b950-a35c56b36c75":{"id":"e8479ff8-f732-4acd-b950-a35c56b36c75","message":{"id":"e8479ff8-f732-4acd-b950-a35c56b36c75","author":{"role":"tool","name":"web","metadata":{}},"create_time":1742610942.575429,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"code","language":"unknown","response_format_name":null,"text":""},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"weight":0,"metadata":{"is_visually_hidden_from_conversation":true,"command":"search","status":"finished","is_complete":true,"message_type":null,"model_slug":"gpt-4o","default_model_slug":"gpt-4o","parent_id":"104a4324-1151-4f35-a489-92b40fc5e094","request_id":"92424bf76f020001-ORD","timestamp_":"absolute"},"recipient":"assistant","channel":null},"parent":"104a4324-1151-4f35-a489-92b40fc5e094","children":["38a4f7bc-e1f6-454a-80d7-eac772d9bcab"]},"38a4f7bc-e1f6-454a-80d7-eac772d9bcab":{"id":"38a4f7bc-e1f6-454a-80d7-eac772d9bcab","message":{"id":"38a4f7bc-e1f6-454a-80d7-eac772d9bcab","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{"real_author":"tool:web"}},"create_time":1742610942.5758646,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"text","parts":["The **electric coolant pump** in your BMW E90 is integral to the engine's cooling system, ensuring optimal operating temperatures. It's controlled by the Digital Motor Electronics (DME) module and communicates over the Bit-Serial Data (BSD) bus, which also interfaces with components like the alternator and Intelligent Battery Sensor (IBS). Faults in the BSD bus can disrupt communication among these components, leading to various error codes.\n\n**Potential Causes of Multiple Faults:**\n\n- **BSD Bus Disruptions:** Faults such as **2E85** (Electric coolant pump, communication) and **2E8B** (Intelligent Battery Sensor, missing) suggest issues in the BSD communication line. A malfunction here can affect the alternator, coolant pump, and IBS simultaneously.\n\n- **Shared Power Supply Issues:** The coolant pump's operation relies on specific fuses: **F33** powers the pump motor, and **F37** supplies the control circuit for both the thermostat and coolant pump. A fault in these fuses can lead to errors like **2E83** (Electric coolant pump, energy operation). citeturn0search14\n\n- **Electrical Connectors and Grounding:** Loose or corroded connectors, especially at the pump's connector **X6035**, or poor grounding can cause intermittent faults.\n\n**Recommended Diagnostic Steps:**\n\n1. **Inspect Fuses:**\n   - Check fuses **F33** and **F37** in the glove compartment fuse box for continuity and proper seating. Replace any blown fuses.\n\n2. **Examine BSD Bus Integrity:**\n   - Inspect the BSD communication line for damage or disconnections. Ensure all connectors are secure and free from corrosion.\n\n3. **Test Electrical Connections:**\n   - Verify the integrity of the connector **X6035** at the coolant pump. Ensure the ground wire at pin #4 has a solid connection to the chassis ground.\n\n4. **Assess Related Components:**\n   - Check the alternator and IBS for proper operation, as faults here can cascade through the BSD bus, affecting the coolant pump's performance.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nAddressing the faults in your BMW E90 requires a systematic approach, focusing on the BSD communication line, power supplies, and electrical connections. By thoroughly inspecting these areas, you can identify and rectify the root causes of the errors, ensuring the reliable operation of your vehicle's systems. "]},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"weight":1,"metadata":{"search_source":"composer_auto","client_reported_search_source":"composer_auto","search_result_groups":[{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"bimmerfest.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.bimmerfest.com/attachments/bmw-complete-diagnostic-fault-code-list-pdf.761561/","title":"BMW Complete Diagnostic Fault Code List [E36, E46, E90 and more]","snippet":"BMW MS40 MS40 was a new ECU for 